## 4. Domain Model

### 4.1 Core Entities

```
Project
  Id, Name, Description
  OwnerId (→ ApplicationUser)
  CreatedAt, UpdatedAt
  MeasurementPreferenceId (→ MeasurementPreference)
  ICollection<Cabinet> Cabinets

MeasurementPreference
  Id
  DefaultLengthUnit        (MeasurementUnit)
  DefaultMassUnit          (MeasurementUnit)
  DefaultVolumeUnit        (MeasurementUnit)

Cabinet
  Id, Name, Description
  ProjectId (→ Project)
  CabinetType              (Base | Wall | Tall | Island | Custom)
  ExteriorWidth            (Measurement — stored as value+unit pair)
  ExteriorHeight           (Measurement)
  ExteriorDepth            (Measurement)
  ICollection<CabinetComponent> Components
  ICollection<CabinetMaterial> Materials

CabinetComponent
  Id, Name
  CabinetId (→ Cabinet)
  ComponentType            (Box | Door | Drawer | Shelf | FaceFrame | Custom)
  Width, Height, Depth     (Measurement each)
  Quantity                 (int)
  MaterialId? (→ Material)

Material
  Id, Name, Description
  Category                 (Sheet | Solid | Hardware | Finish | Other)
  Thickness                (Measurement — nullable, relevant for sheet goods)
  UnitCost                 (decimal)
  CostUnit                 (MeasurementUnit — e.g., SquareFoot, LinearFoot, Each)

CabinetMaterial
  CabinetId, MaterialId    (join entity)
  EstimatedQuantity        (Measurement)
  Notes
```

### 4.2 Value Object Conventions

`Measurement` is always a struct/record struct. EF Core maps it via owned entity (two columns per measurement). A custom `MeasurementValueConverter` handles serialization. All entity measurement properties use the `[Owned]` attribute or Fluent API `OwnsOne` configuration.

