## 5. Data Access Layer (DAL)

### 5.1 DbContext

`CabinetMakerDbContext` inherits `IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>`. Owned entity mappings for `Measurement` are registered in `OnModelCreating` via a shared extension method `ConfigureMeasurement(builder, prefix)` so column naming is consistent:

```
cabinet.ExteriorWidth → ExteriorWidth_Value, ExteriorWidth_Unit
```

### 5.2 Repository Pattern

Each aggregate root gets a typed repository interface in Domain and an EF implementation in DAL:

```
IProjectRepository  →  ProjectRepository
ICabinetRepository  →  CabinetRepository
IMaterialRepository →  MaterialRepository
```

A `IUnitOfWork` wraps the DbContext and exposes `SaveChangesAsync`. BRL calls repositories through interfaces; DAL wires them up via DI.

### 5.3 Migrations

EF Core migrations live under `DAL/Migrations/`. A `DbInitializer` seeds reference data (default materials, unit conversion factors if persisted) on first run in Development.

