## 7. Web / UI Layer

### 7.1 Blazor Render Mode

**Interactive Server** render mode (already configured in `Program.cs`). All interactive components use `@rendermode InteractiveServer`. Static SSR is used for read-only pages (project list landing, print views).

### 7.2 MVVM Approach — CommunityToolkit.Mvvm

**Recommendation: use `CommunityToolkit.Mvvm`** (Microsoft-maintained, source-generator based, zero runtime overhead, works perfectly in Blazor).

Key features used:
- `ObservableObject` base class (or `[ObservableProperty]` source gen attribute)
- `[RelayCommand]` for async commands
- `IMessenger` / `WeakReferenceMessenger` for cross-component communication

ViewModel pattern in Blazor:

```
ProjectListViewModel    ↔  ProjectListPage.razor
ProjectDetailViewModel  ↔  ProjectDetailPage.razor
CabinetEditorViewModel  ↔  CabinetEditorPage.razor
MeasurementInputViewModel ↔ MeasurementInput.razor (shared component)
```

Each `.razor` page injects its ViewModel as a scoped service. The ViewModel exposes properties and commands; the Razor template binds to them. `StateHasChanged()` is triggered via a thin `ComponentBase` base class (`ViewModelComponentBase<TViewModel>`) that subscribes to `PropertyChanged`.

```csharp
// ViewModelComponentBase<T> pattern
protected override void OnInitialized()
    => ViewModel.PropertyChanged += (_, _) => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
```

### 7.3 Component Hierarchy

```
Pages/
  Projects/
    ProjectList.razor         (lists all projects)
    ProjectDetail.razor       (project overview, cabinet list)
  Cabinets/
    CabinetEditor.razor       (create/edit cabinet + components)
    CabinetSummary.razor      (read-only card view)
  Reports/
    CutList.razor             (printable cut list)
    MaterialEstimate.razor    (cost summary)
Shared/
  MeasurementInput.razor      (unit-aware numeric input field)
  MeasurementDisplay.razor    (formatted read-only display)
  UnitSelector.razor          (dropdown for unit selection)
  ResultAlert.razor           (maps Result<T> errors to Bootstrap alerts)
Layout/
  MainLayout.razor
  NavMenu.razor
```

### 7.4 Bootstrap Theme

Bootstrap 5.x via CDN or npm (LibMan). Custom CSS variables override the Bootstrap palette to give the app a woodwork/craft aesthetic (warm neutrals, no neon accents). No custom component library — Bootstrap utility classes + minimal component-level `<style>` blocks only.

